#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Predecoded Marble Madness course, collision, tile and palette data.

No ROM ZIP is read or required by this module. Arrays were decoded once from
user-supplied reference data into native game structures and embedded below.
The translated game engine reads compact native data tables from
``marble_tables.py``; neither the emulator nor a ROM file is needed.

Data model:
  race words: (playfield rows, 36), uint16 tile/palette/flip codes
  collision heights: (height rows, 22, 4), int32 corners
  playfield tiles: (4096, 8, 8), uint8 pixel indices 0..31
  sprite tiles: (2048, 8, 8), uint8 pixel indices 0..7
  palettes: six RGB (128, 3) playfield and (8, 8, 3) sprite palettes

Data is deflate-compressed and Base85-text encoded to keep one manageable
.py file instead of thousands of literal integer lists. This is not a
reproduction of the Atari program ROM or a CPU/graphics-ROM decoder.

Important: Derivative graphics and level layouts may still be copyright
protected; converting them to Python does NOT confer redistribution rights.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

